 faq=[("Is there a game in the app too?","Yes: five courses, steered by tilting the phone. It’s a game with simplified physics, not training."),
  ("How does steering by tilting the phone work?","Hold the phone however is comfortable: its position during the countdown becomes neutral. Tilt left or right to put the board on its edge and turn. Tip the top away from you for more speed. A finger on the screen squats, and letting go jumps. If tilt isn’t for you, you can steer with a finger instead."),
  ("Can you learn to snowboard from an app?","You can learn what each move is and what it does: how weight moves, why the nose drops, when the edge changes. Feeling it takes snow, so learn new moves with an instructor and use the app to prepare."),
  ("How do I start if I have never been on a board?","Start with level one: the rules on the slope, and how to fall and get up. Then the board and your stance, pushing with one foot and your first glides."),
  ("How do you turn on a snowboard?","The app teaches this order: weight toward the leading foot, leading foot flat so the nose drops to the fall line, hips to the new edge, then flex and steer with the leading knee and hip. You can watch each step in slow motion, then steer it yourself on the model."),
  ("Why does my edge catch?","In one common case, the new edge goes down while the board still points across the slope. The snow stops the edge and your body keeps going. So: nose into the fall line first, edge change after. The app shows this mistake next to the correct move."),
  ("How should I fall on a snowboard?","Forward, onto your knees and forearms. Backward, onto your seat and back. The falling lesson shows both in 3D, along with what your arms mustn’t do and how to get up. No technique guarantees a safe fall, and instructors strongly recommend a helmet."),
  ("Regular or goofy: how do I know my stance?","The app asks which foot leads. If you don’t know yet, it shows an example stance, clearly labeled, and you can change it later. Your writing hand doesn’t decide your stance."),
  ("Does the app use the camera or rate my riding?","No. It doesn’t use the camera, there are no sensors on your board, and it can’t see how you ride. The score in the steering exercises is about the model only. It isn’t a skill rating."),
  ("Does it need internet or an account?","No. It works offline, with no account, ads, analytics or tracking. Your progress, notes and best scores stay on your iPhone."),
  ("Which devices and languages does it support?","iPhone with iOS 18 or later. English, Russian, German, French, Spanish, Italian, Simplified Chinese, Japanese and Korean."),
  ("When is it out, and how does it work?","The app is being prepared for the App Store. It works on a one-time purchase, with no subscription. Details will be on its App Store page.")],
